8\. Bluetooth spoofing

A device impersonates another Bluetooth device or uses a misleading device identity.

Testing tools: Bluetoothctl, Wireshark, btmon.

Safe test: Inspect the Bluetooth devices visible to your own computer and verify their identities.

![Störungen im Luftverkehr - Swiss ist täglich von GPS-Spoofing betroffen - News - SRF](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/cGV5TVKREOJhoIA1mahBXx-toqV84GXrg33Uyb4CtxN8A-_gqDXvws2cbI3aaZURlnAKaWXdSSo8OIwesusLyzr-GvOzeoNeDCBGLQYt9ngxDLeKLRaIZyRaTe3wnHaxOBdd22TiQx9JWyHKYbD8oewSyqDZw65j3kJpigVP14NbC2owXMbPGRwwLwSdfeyi?purpose=fullsize)

9\. GPS spoofing

False satellite-like signals attempt to make a GPS receiver calculate an incorrect position or time.

Testing tools: GNSS monitoring software and simulated GNSS receivers.

Safe test: Use recorded or simulated GNSS data and compare the calculated position with the known reference position.

