### 4\. How to know whether spoofing is successful

When testing your own systems, look for these indicators:

| Attack           | Possible warning sign                             |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
| IP spoofing      | Source address inconsistent with network location |
| ARP spoofing     | Unexpected IP-to-MAC changes                      |
| DNS spoofing     | Unexpected DNS responses                          |
| MAC spoofing     | Duplicate MAC addresses or unexpected changes     |
| DHCP spoofing    | Unauthorized DHCP server                          |
| Evil Twin        | Duplicate SSID with an unauthorized BSSID         |
| Email spoofing   | SPF, DKIM or DMARC failure                        |
| Website spoofing | Incorrect domain or suspicious certificate        |
| Session spoofing | Unauthorized session reuse                        |
| GPS spoofing     | Position inconsistent with trusted reference      |

For DNS security, DNSSEC validation and trusted resolver configuration are important protections. Canadian Centre for Cyber Security +2

